{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792311233,"nonce":"ODCrk82zmmlW493HbgmP83as050=","message":"Diagnosis (reproduced with ashui's xwindow.wasm, blinc_abi.wasm and xgpu.wasm, probe ThreadWake): not about which library is bound. The web build of window_wake is only 'call hl_xidl::host::throw_pending; return 0', and throw_pending reads a Rust thread_local (RefCell\u003cOption\u003cString\u003e\u003e) at __tls_base + 184. xwindow.wasm has (start $__wasm_init_memory): the first instance copies .rodata/.data, sets its own __tls_base global to a static TLS block inside the library's memory (memory_base + 16384, 280 bytes of .tdata then 120 of .tbss) and sets an init flag; every later instance, i.e. every thread's, finds the flag set and leaves __tls_base at 0. wasm-ld gives a shared library no __wasm_init_tls, so there is nothing for a loader to call. A thread therefore reads 'its' thread-locals at address 0+offset of the program's memory and sees garbage, hence the empty ValueException. blinc_abi works on a thread because its natives use no thread-local. Fix in progress in the loader: export the library's __tls_base global, capture the pristine TLS image from the first instance (after relocations, before constructors), and give each thread instance its own malloc'd copy with __tls_base set to it, on both hosts.","files":null}]}